The Ministry of Education and Research, through the National Center for Curriculum and Evaluation, announces the launch in the process of institutional transparency of a new set of 175 school programs for high school education, developed as part of the curriculum reform process. It complements the school programs previously approved by the Order of the Minister of Education no. 6.930/2025 (87 programs), by Order of the Minister of Education and Research no. 3.224/2026 (3 programs) and by the Order of the Minister of Education and Research no. 3.716/2026 (320 programs).

The 175 school programs proposed for public consultation cover the following categories:

A. School programs for compulsory subjects with hourly allocation in the specialized curriculum (CS) for high school education, vocational stream, pedagogical profile

67 school programs were developed for the specialized subjects from the specialized curriculum (CS), related to the vocational stream, the pedagogical profile, for all five specializations:

early education;

pedagogy of primary education;

general pedagogy;

school mediation;

pedagogy of non-formal education.

B. School programs for compulsory subjects with hourly allocation in the common core (TC) and/or in the specialized curriculum (CS)

23 school programs were developed for the following subjects:

Physics;

Biology;

History;

Psychology;

Sociology;

Philosophy;

Social studies;

Economics and entrepreneurship education.

C. School programs for compulsory subjects with hourly allocation in the specialized curriculum (CS) for the technological stream

24 school programs were developed for the specialized curriculum related to the 10th grade, for all profiles and the main areas of professional training in the technological sector, including:

constructions, installations and public works;

electric;

electromechanics;

mechanics;

agriculture;

food industry;

tourism and food;

economic;

trade;

environmental protection;

automation electronics;

media production.

D. School programs for compulsory subjects with hourly allocation in the common core (tc) and/or the specialized curriculum (CS) - education in the language of national minorities

40 school programs were developed for the mother tongue and literature, as well as for specialized subjects intended for high school education in the languages of national minorities, including:

Bulgarian language;

Czech;

German;

Hungarian;

Neo-Greek language;

Romani language;

Serbian;

Slovak language;

Turkish;

Ukrainian.

E. School programs for compulsory subjects with hourly allocation in the common core (TC) and/or the specialized curriculum (CS) - modern languages

8 school programs were developed for modern languages, including for classes with modern language teaching in a bilingual regime, based on inter-governmental agreements, as well as for non-linguistic subjects, including:

Chinese language;

Hebrew;

the english language

French, including bilingual;

Italian language, including bilingual;

Portuguese;

Spanish language, including bilingual;

Turkish.

F. School programs for compulsory subjects with hourly allocation in the specialized curriculum (CS) - theoretical stream and vocational stream

7 school programs were developed for subjects from the specialized curriculum, such as:

universal literature;

I KNEW;

the history of ballet;

individual repertoire

G. School programs for compulsory subjects with hourly allocation in the common core (TC) and/or in the specialized curriculum (CS)

6 school programs were developed for the following subjects:

Romanian language and literature, 10th - 12th grades;

Romanian language and literature for schools and sections with teaching in the Hungarian language, 9th - 12th grades.

H. Continuity of the curriculum development process

The Ministry of Education and Research, through the National Center for Curriculum and Evaluation, states that the process of developing and approving school programs for high school education continues, following new stages of public consultation and approval, in order to fully complete the curriculum related to the new framework plans for high school, including for special high school education.

Possible proposals and observations can be sent within the next 10 calendar days to the e-mail address consultare @ rocnee.ro.

Also, opinions and possible proposals can be submitted by filling in the google forms, available ► here (for the general public), respectively ► here (for teachers).

Projects subject to the consultation/transparency process are published ► HERE.

